\f0\b\fs58\fsmilli29333 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 CWO Admin Tool \'97 How to Use\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f1\i\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \strokec3 Owner-only admin interface for live Cthulhu Wars Online games on cwo.freeddns.org.
\f2\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa365\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs44 \cf2 \strokec2 Quick start\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Open 
\f3 admin.html
\f2  in this folder by double-clicking it. It opens in your default browser.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Server URL is pre-filled to 
\f3 https://cwo.freeddns.org
\f2 . Leave it.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Paste your owner admin token (kept in 
\f3 Server Deployment/owner-admin-token.txt
\f2  in the Library at Celaeno folder).\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Click 
\f0\b Sign in
\f2\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0
\cf0 You'll see a list of all live games. Click any game to view its players and log.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa365\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs44 \cf2 \strokec2 What you can do\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa343\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17160 \cf0 \strokec3 See all live games\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 Left column lists every active game on the server by its natural-language name (e.g. "Disaster and Space"). Each game has an 
\f0\b Open as Owner
\f2\b0  button that takes you straight into the game with the master secret \'97 so you see every faction and every detail.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa343\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17160 \cf0 See a game's players\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 Click a game in the left column. The right column shows each faction in the game with a clickable link. Clicking a faction opens that player's view (using their secret URL) \'97 so you can step in and play on their behalf.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa343\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17160 \cf0 Read the game log\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 Below the players, you see every log entry in the game in reverse order (most recent at top). Each line shows its index, the role that wrote it, and the action.\
Lines in red contain dice rolls, Elder Signs, Silence Tokens, or captures \'97 events that are normally permanent and blocked from undo by regular players. As the owner, you can roll back past any line.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa343\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17160 \cf0 Roll back the game\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 Every log line has a 
\f0\b Roll back to here
\f2\b0  button. Click it to delete that line and everything after. A confirmation dialog appears first. After rollback, refresh and you'll see the truncated log. Now reload the game from the player's perspective (via the player link) and pick up from there.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa343\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17160 \cf0 Replay deleted entries\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 If you rolled back to fix a UI bug and want to put the game back exactly where it was, just re-do the actions from inside the game (loading as the appropriate player). The game will accept them as normal player actions and re-record them. If a dice roll or Elder Sign is involved, it will re-roll/re-draw randomly \'97 you can manually edit the log entry to match the original if needed (advanced use).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa365\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs44 \cf2 \strokec2 Security notes\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 The owner token is the ONLY thing protecting these admin endpoints. Treat it like an email password.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 If the token leaks, anyone who has it can wipe every game on the server. Rotate it by editing one line on the server.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 The token is stored at 
\f3 Library at Celaeno/Server Deployment/owner-admin-token.txt
\f2  on this machine (chmod 600).\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 The admin endpoints return HTTP 404 to anyone without the token \'97 so probing for them returns the same response as a non-existent URL. No way to tell admin is enabled by external observation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa365\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs44 \cf2 \strokec2 Token rotation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa293\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \strokec3 If you ever want to change the token:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Generate a new one: in Terminal, run 
\f3 openssl rand -hex 24
\f2  and copy the output.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Update 
\f3 /etc/systemd/system/cwo.service
\f2  on the VM \'97 the systemd ExecStart line has the token as the last argv.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Save the new token to the local 
\f3 owner-admin-token.txt
\f2  file.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 SSH to the VM: 
\f3 sudo systemctl daemon-reload && sudo systemctl restart cwo
\f2 .\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Sign in to 
\f3 admin.html
\f2  with the new token.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa365\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs44 \cf2 \strokec2 Limitations of this v1\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f2\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 You can't see a faction's CURRENT state in a nice table \'97 only by opening their player view. Reconstructing the live game state from the log requires running the engine. The "Open as Owner" or "Open as <faction>" buttons give you that without leaving the admin tool.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 You can't directly edit a log entry from the admin. You can roll back and re-do. To literally rewrite an entry's text, edit the database directly on the VM (advanced).\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 The admin page is loaded locally from this folder \'97 if you want to access it from another device, copy this folder over (it's self-contained).\
}